######## open questions that name what they block

  mixed_numeral_addition   [decider: op]
      A large part of one cluster has no caller if the answer is no. `23`'s words, carried in the 
      register: \"One sentence from op collapses it.\"

  arithmetic_column_one_axis_or_two   [decider: op]
      Prior to Q6, because it decides what a wrap-or-clamp answer would be an answer about.

  the_width_surface_crossing   [decider: op]
      What a consumer writes at every arithmetic call site under the seventh option, which is outside 
      where the ratified ergonomics bar was written to govern.

  does_precision_count_the_sign_digit   [decider: op]
      What the sign domain moves; whether the three sign domains at equal precision form a chain or 
      leave one incomparable; whether the symmetric domain at precision one denotes exactly the zero 
      set, which bears on whether a zero-width numeral already exists under one reading; and whether 
      two of the three sign domains collapse at an odd radix.

  is_the_role_set_closed   [decider: panel]
      Op's plural in \"numeral representations\", which the role set is what explains.

  which_reassociated_arm_a_law_licenses   [decider: measurement]
      Whether an instruction count may be used as a cost model anywhere in this corpus, which this 
      entry measures it cannot be.

  which_operation_set_the_design_ships   [decider: op]
      The preset count and their names, which is op's own open intent. The topic's result is that it 
      cannot be closed from below, because it is downstream of this, so this one question is the 
      whole of that one. It also decides whether footprint is observable, and with it one clause of 
      the primitive candidate, the contested one-vocabulary-or-two fork, and whether the count of 
      primitives is container-relative.

  may_the_canon_carry_an_unpredicated_proposition   [decider: op]
      The form of every canon sentence, in every topic, including the ones already written. The 
      largest of the queue's items in reach and the cheapest to answer.

  is_the_rounding_candidates_pairing_section_canon_or_design   [decider: op]
      The same line in every other topic, since each candidate has drawn it by instinct and none has 
      had it confirmed. Answering it once fixes it everywhere.

  why_the_default_rounding_position_is_chosen   [decider: op]
      Whether the rounding topic's arms are reachable at the default, which is the difference between 
      an arm that exists and an arm anyone will ever hit.

  which_units_a_weighting_is_expressed_in   [decider: op]
      Whether a weighting travels.

  the_rounding_mode_vocabulary   [decider: op]
      Nothing structural. It is in the queue because naming is op's taste and taste does not converge 
      by argument, so it will sit forever unless it is asked.

  the_container_premise   [decider: op]
      The statement of what a primitive is, which is the panel's central noun and which four topics 
      have deferred to.

  does_the_observability_principle_become_an_intent   [decider: op]
      The ground under the tenth unit's licence clause, that everything inside an unobserved stretch 
      is arvo's to choose.

  does_a_named_policy_selection_survive_above_the_numeral   [decider: panel]
      Whether the strategy shape is a numeral-local thing or a general one, which decides what a 
      composition contract may carry.

